---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// V-691 — profiles developer docs. Companion to /docs/sessions;
// covers the saved-profile lifecycle for customers running
// repeatable, identity-bound automations.

const SAMPLE_PROFILE = `{
  "id": "prof_…",
  "name": "us-east-sales-bot",
  "archetype": "default",
  "user_agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) ...",
  "viewport": { "width": 1280, "height": 800 },
  "locale": "en-US",
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "cookies_persisted": true,
  "created_at": "2026-05-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00.000Z"
}`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Profiles API — Driftstack developer docs" description="Saved browser profiles for repeatable, identity-bound automations.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 prose prose-slate dark:prose-invert">
    <h1>Profiles</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      A profile is a saved browser identity — user agent, viewport,
      locale, timezone, persisted cookies. Sessions can either run
      ad-hoc (with a built-in archetype) or be pinned to a saved
      profile for consistent identity across runs.
    </p>

    <h2>When to use a profile</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Authenticated scraping.</strong> The site requires
        login; you want the session to carry over so each run doesn't
        need to re-authenticate.</li>
      <li><strong>A/B-tested rendering.</strong> The site personalises
        based on cookies; you want to consistently see the same
        variant across runs.</li>
      <li><strong>Geographic + locale fidelity.</strong> You're
        automating against a region-locked feature and need the
        browser fingerprint to match.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If your automation doesn't care about identity continuity, skip
      profiles and let sessions use the default archetype.
    </p>

    <h2>POST /v1/profiles — mint</h2>
    <pre><code>{`POST /v1/profiles
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "us-east-sales-bot",
  "archetype": "default",                 ← starting point
  "viewport": { "width": 1280, "height": 800 },
  "locale": "en-US",
  "timezone": "America/New_York",
  "cookies_persisted": true               ← keep cookies across sessions
}

→ 201 Created
${SAMPLE_PROFILE}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      <code>archetype</code> selects the base preset (see
      <a href="/docs/sessions">the sessions docs</a> for the list).
      Subsequent fields override the archetype's defaults.
    </p>

    <h2>GET /v1/profiles — list</h2>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/profiles?limit=25
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 200 OK
{
  "profiles": [...],
  "nextCursor": "cur_…"
}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>GET /v1/profiles/:id</h2>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/profiles/prof_…
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 200 OK
${SAMPLE_PROFILE}`}</code></pre>

    <h2>PATCH /v1/profiles/:id — update</h2>
    <pre><code>{`PATCH /v1/profiles/prof_…
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "us-east-sales-bot-v2",
  "viewport": { "width": 1440, "height": 900 }
}

→ 200 OK
${SAMPLE_PROFILE}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Only the fields you supply are updated. The
      <code>cookies_persisted</code> flag is sticky — you cannot flip
      it back to <code>false</code> after a session has written
      cookies; you'd need to delete + re-mint the profile.
    </p>

    <h2>DELETE /v1/profiles/:id</h2>
    <pre><code>{`DELETE /v1/profiles/prof_…
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ 204 No Content`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Persisted cookies + storage state are deleted. In-flight
      sessions that started with this profile keep running but
      can't be pinned to it again. Idempotent: a second DELETE on
      the same id returns 204.
    </p>

    <h2>Snapshot history (V-312)</h2>
    <p>
      Profile snapshots record the cookies + storage state at the
      end of each session that used the profile. Customers can
      restore a previous snapshot if the current state is broken
      (e.g. the site logged the profile out):
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`GET /v1/profiles/prof_…/snapshots
Authorization: Bearer ds_live_…

→ {
  "snapshots": [
    { "id": "snap_…", "captured_at": "2026-05-11T11:00:00.000Z" },
    ...
  ]
}

POST /v1/profiles/prof_…/snapshots/snap_…/restore
→ 200 OK { "restored": true }`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Snapshots are kept for 30 days. Older snapshots are pruned
      automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy + retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cookies + storage state stored in encrypted form at rest.</li>
      <li>Profile + snapshots deleted on account deletion + 30 days
        after the most recent customer-initiated DELETE.</li>
      <li>No identifying customer data is included in the profile
        fingerprint — the browser fingerprint is what you configure.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      Max profiles per account: 50 (Solo Manual / API Starter), 250
      (Team Manual / API Builder), 1000 (API Scale). Need more?
      Email <a href="mailto:support@driftstack.dev">support</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Support</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:developers@driftstack.dev">developers@driftstack.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
